<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<layout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <!--
      COLLECTION, migrated to the frozen 3.6.6 canonical design (Phase B).

      Source: the canonical `COLLECTION` / `COLLECTION_dark` and `COLLECTION
      pusto` / `COLLECTION pusto_dark` frames. All four are 390x740 with
      identical geometry - only the fills differ - so one layout serves both
      themes and both states:

        Header - TopAppBar   0..64    "Моя коллекция", trailing overflow
        subtitle             y=80     "Здесь хранятся ваши сохранённые треки"
        list / empty card    y=132
        Main ends            612      after a 154 bottom padding

      Three structural notes.

      **The outer card is gone.** The screen used to put everything inside one
      #0F253E MaterialCardView with 40dp side margins. The frozen design has no
      such container: the rows are the cards, on the plain `background` role. The
      empty state is the one card the frozen design does draw, and it is drawn to
      the same radius, surface and stroke as a track row.

      **The subtitle does not scroll.** It is 20 tall and the frozen `Main` does
      not scroll at all; scrolling it away would mean a header view type in
      FavoritesAdapter, which is behaviour this re-skin does not touch. The list
      below it scrolls, and it is the list that carries the clearance.

      **Nothing here draws the Mini Player.** It lives on the shell (B2), already
      lists "favorites" among the screens it appears on, and is untouched by this
      migration. All this screen owes it is the 154 of bottom clearance the
      frozen `Main` reserves.
    -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/collection_root"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:background="@color/background"
        android:orientation="vertical"
        tools:context=".fragments.FavoritesFragment">

        <!--
          Header - TopAppBar, 390x64: the title vertically centred 16 from
          the leading edge, the overflow on the trailing one.

          The frozen `COLLECTION pusto` header carries a 40x40 circular
          control in that trailing slot instead of the overflow. It is the
          same node HOME and ABOUT US carry and it opens the profile.

          Landed in G-A3, and the two controls are mutually exclusive, which is
          the part worth stating: the FINAL Figma file gives the profile control
          to `COLLECTION pusto` (2429:352 / 2444:18515) and gives the populated
          frames (2399:31129 / 2444:18376) the three-dot overflow instead. So the
          empty state shows the profile control and the populated state shows the
          overflow, never both - FavoritesFragment toggles them together against
          the same emptiness that already decided the overflow.
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/collection_header"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/collection_header_height"
            android:gravity="center_vertical"
            android:orientation="horizontal"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/collection_margin"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/collection_margin">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/title"
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:text="@string/collection_title"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Montserrat.Medium.24_32"
                android:textColor="@color/text_heading" />

            <!--
              The frozen 3-dot overflow. Phase B fills it with the two export
              actions the screen already had as inline pills, in a platform
              PopupMenu; F2 replaces that styling with the frozen
              `Menu / Коллекция` surface. It is hidden while the collection
              is empty, which is what the frozen empty frame does too - there
              is nothing to export.
            -->
            <ImageView
                android:id="@+id/collection_overflow"
                android:layout_width="@dimen/collection_header_action_size"
                android:layout_height="@dimen/collection_header_action_size"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackgroundBorderless"
                android:contentDescription="@string/collection_overflow"
                android:scaleType="center"
                android:src="@drawable/ic_collection_overflow" />

            <!--
              GONE by default, which is the populated state - the mirror of the
              overflow above, whose layout default is VISIBLE for the same reason.
              FavoritesFragment swaps the pair when it learns the collection is
              empty; until it does, the header must already be the populated one or
              the overflow is pushed 40dp off its frozen trailing anchor.
            -->
            <include
                android:id="@+id/settings_entry"
                layout="@layout/view_settings_entry"
                android:visibility="gone" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/collection_subtitle"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/collection_header_gap"
            android:gravity="center_vertical"
            android:minHeight="@dimen/collection_subtitle_min_height"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/collection_margin"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/collection_margin"
            android:text="@string/collection_subtitle"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Regular.14_20"
            android:textColor="@color/text_secondary" />

        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/collection_section_gap"
            android:layout_weight="1">

            <!--
              clipToPadding=false on both children, so the reserved bottom
              clearance is scroll room rather than a dead band and the last
              row can be brought clear of the Mini Player.
            -->
            <androidx.recyclerview.widget.RecyclerView
                android:id="@+id/rv_favorites"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:clipToPadding="false"
                android:paddingStart="@dimen/collection_margin"
                android:paddingEnd="@dimen/collection_margin"
                android:paddingBottom="@dimen/content_bottom_clearance"
                android:scrollbars="none"
                tools:listitem="@layout/item_favorite_track" />

            <androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView
                android:id="@+id/empty_state"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:clipToPadding="false"
                android:paddingStart="@dimen/collection_margin"
                android:paddingEnd="@dimen/collection_margin"
                android:paddingBottom="@dimen/content_bottom_clearance"
                android:scrollbars="none"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible">

                <!--
                  A wrapper, and it is load-bearing. NestedScrollView measures
                  its one direct child with an UNSPECIFIED height whatever that
                  child's layout_height says, so a fixed 359 put straight on
                  the card is discarded and the card wraps its content instead.
                  The wrapper takes the UNSPECIFIED and the card keeps its
                  frozen height inside it.
                -->
                <FrameLayout
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                    <!--
                      The frozen empty card: 358x359, the same surface, radius and
                      stroke as a track row, with absolutely-positioned children.

                      The two text blocks are centred on their frozen box centres
                      rather than anchored on their tops - see dimens.xml for why
                      the boxes themselves cannot be reproduced literally.
                    -->
                    <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
                        android:id="@+id/empty_card"
                        style="@style/CollectionCard"
                        android:layout_height="@dimen/collection_empty_card_height">

                        <androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="match_parent">

                            <androidx.constraintlayout.widget.Guideline
                                android:id="@+id/empty_title_center"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:orientation="horizontal"
                                app:layout_constraintGuide_begin="@dimen/collection_empty_title_center" />

                            <androidx.constraintlayout.widget.Guideline
                                android:id="@+id/empty_body_center"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:orientation="horizontal"
                                app:layout_constraintGuide_begin="@dimen/collection_empty_body_center" />

                            <ImageView
                                android:id="@+id/empty_illustration"
                                android:layout_width="@dimen/collection_empty_illustration_size"
                                android:layout_height="@dimen/collection_empty_illustration_size"
                                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/collection_empty_illustration_top"
                                android:contentDescription="@string/collection_empty_illustration"
                                android:src="@drawable/ic_collection_empty"
                                app:layout_constraintEnd_toEndOf="parent"
                                app:layout_constraintStart_toStartOf="parent"
                                app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="parent" />

                            <TextView
                                android:id="@+id/empty_title"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:gravity="center"
                                android:minHeight="@dimen/collection_empty_title_min_height"
                                android:text="@string/collection_empty_title"
                                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Medium.16_28"
                                android:textColor="@color/text_primary"
                                app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="@id/empty_title_center"
                                app:layout_constraintEnd_toEndOf="parent"
                                app:layout_constraintStart_toStartOf="parent"
                                app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="@id/empty_title_center" />

                            <!--
                              Two things about this line.

                              Its light colour on the canonical page is #000000,
                              which is an outlier: every other secondary line in
                              the same frame, the header subtitle included, is
                              #42474E, and the dark page has this one on #B3C4D1,
                              which is exactly text_secondary. One role, both
                              themes.

                              And the box hugs its two lines rather than taking the
                              frozen 191. That 191 is a Muller measurement, Onest
                              sets this string wider, and pinning it forced a third
                              line - which breaks the two-line block the frozen
                              frame draws. The copy carries its own line break, so
                              hugging keeps exactly the frozen break and the frozen
                              centre while letting the replacement font have the
                              width it needs; the same licensing-driven metric
                              delta docs/TYPOGRAPHY-3.6.6.md records elsewhere.

                              The box is the card minus a 16 inset on each side
                              and the text is centred inside it, rather than the
                              box hugging the text. Hugging needs
                              layout_constrainedWidth to stay inside the card,
                              and that is a two-pass measure which settled 10px
                              narrower than the line it had to hold on API 24 -
                              a real overflow, caught by the width sweep. A
                              fixed box has no second pass to disagree with, and
                              centred text puts the block in exactly the same
                              place.
                            -->
                            <TextView
                                android:id="@+id/empty_body"
                                android:layout_width="0dp"
                                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/collection_margin"
                                android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/collection_margin"
                                android:gravity="center"
                                android:minHeight="@dimen/collection_empty_body_min_height"
                                android:text="@string/collection_empty_body"
                                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Regular.12_20"
                                android:textColor="@color/text_secondary"
                                app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="@id/empty_body_center"
                                app:layout_constraintEnd_toEndOf="parent"
                                app:layout_constraintStart_toStartOf="parent"
                                app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="@id/empty_body_center" />

                        </androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout>

                    </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

                </FrameLayout>

            </androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>

        </FrameLayout>

    </LinearLayout>

</layout>
